	•	Section 3 Comments/Quotes: The paper developed “ToPs: Trees of Predictors,” an interpretable method that clusters patients and assigns different predictive models to different clusters. Inputs were tabular recipient, donor, and compatibility variables from UNOS. The main comparators were existing clinical risk scores such as DRI, RSS, and IMPACT, so Linear Risk Score is the closest label. Validation used 5-fold cross-validation. Explainability was intrinsic through the tree structure and cluster-specific relevant features, even though SHAP/LIME was not used. Feature selection was automated by excluding features with high missingness and then learning predictive clusters and relevant covariates from the data. Explicit hyperparameter tuning was not described in the retrieved text.  ￼

