	•	Section 4 Comments/Quotes: Missing feature components were handled using “10 multiple imputations using Multiple Imputation by Chained Equations (MICE).” Preprocessing included exclusion of post-transplant-only variables, removal of features with >10% missingness, binarization of categorical variables, and 5-fold cross-validation. Since the design used cross-validation on large cohorts rather than a single fixed split, training and test N are NR. Class imbalance is not especially applicable for these survival-prediction settings as reported here. I did not identify a code-release statement.  ￼

